  "split_rationale": "The four ABL entries available (2G1T, 2HZ4, 2V7A, 8SSN) all share UniProt P00519 and therefore one homolog group, so they cannot straddle the splits. Both feature-richest candidates are ABL, so the group is confined to held_out, which also puts the harder cases where generalization is tested. 4HHB is deliberately not used here: it shares the haemoglobin group with AF-P69905, which the alphafold stratum needs, and the leakage rule applies across strata within a panel. The alphafold stratum uses four distinct homolog groups, none shared with the x-ray cases. The globin group is committed to held_out by AF-P69905, which means 4HHB (human deoxyhaemoglobin) can never enter an x-ray development split without leaking that group across the two.",
